{"id":"promise-walk-request","promise":"The Queen requested a private walk with the lady-in-waiting and discussed loneliness in roles not of their choosing.","scene":"s-001","quote":"\"One thing,\" she said, when the ledger had been read and the butler's voice had returned to its neutral cadence. \"I should like a walk. The Long Walk, if you please.\"","dueByScene":"s-001","paidOffBy":null}
{"id":"pc-noted-kitchen-choice","promise":"The butler will keep the household flexible for the Queen's absence and the kitchen prepared a cold tray (sliced cold chicken, open sandwiches and fruit) in case she returned hungry.","scene":"s-001","quote":"\"We will make provisions. I will keep the household flexible. The kitchen will put together something—sliced cold chicken, open sandwiches and fruit—should you return hungry.","dueByScene":"s-001","paidOffBy":null}
